Chapter: RealLiteralRounding

 `__text_to_double` accumulated the digits as one integer and then divided by
 ten once per fractional digit, in a loop. IEEE-754 division rounds once, so
 a loop of them rounds once per digit, and the result drifts from the
 correctly rounded value. `2.9000001` came out one ulp low, and 106 of the
 580 distinct decimal literals in the tree were affected, pi and tau among
 them. Ten to the power k is exact as a double for k up to 22, so
 accumulating the divisor and dividing once is correctly rounded across the
 whole range a literal can usefully name.

 THE FIVE BOUNDARY LITERALS ADDED BELOW ARE THE REGRESSION TARGET FOR
 COMPILER-57, and three of them are RED AT HEAD ON PURPOSE. The divisor fix
 above is correct; the significand conversion is not -- the digits accumulate
 into an i64 and cvtsi2sd makes that an f64, exact only below 2^53, so a literal
 needing 16 or more significant digits rounds twice and lands one ULP off. The
 .expected values are the CORRECTLY ROUNDED bits, so 11.700000000000001,
 97.59752277630605 and 993.1027217047139 mismatch until the parser rounds once;
 0.123456789012345 (15 digits) and 5.8500000000000005 stay green -- the latter
 shows the defect is data-dependent, rounding the right way where its sibling
 11.7 does not.

Section: Report

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    print-line-uni ("2.9000001 " & show (real-to-bits 2.9000001))
    print-line-uni ("3.141592654 " & show (real-to-bits 3.141592654))
    print-line-uni ("6.283185307 " & show (real-to-bits 6.283185307))
    print-line-uni ("1.570796327 " & show (real-to-bits 1.570796327))
    print-line-uni ("0.707 " & show (real-to-bits 0.707))
    print-line-uni ("1.047 " & show (real-to-bits 1.047))
    print-line-uni ("2.22 " & show (real-to-bits 2.22))
    print-line-uni ("0.17 " & show (real-to-bits 0.17))
    print-line-uni ("1.333 " & show (real-to-bits 1.333))
    print-line-uni ("1.5 " & show (real-to-bits 1.5))
    print-line-uni ("0.5 " & show (real-to-bits 0.5))
    print-line-uni ("0.25 " & show (real-to-bits 0.25))
    print-line-uni ("0.123456789012345 " & show (real-to-bits 0.123456789012345))
    print-line-uni ("5.8500000000000005 " & show (real-to-bits 5.8500000000000005))
    print-line-uni ("11.700000000000001 " & show (real-to-bits 11.700000000000001))
    print-line-uni ("97.59752277630605 " & show (real-to-bits 97.59752277630605))
    print-line-uni ("993.1027217047139 " & show (real-to-bits 993.1027217047139))
  end
